    kind: work_item  # 572c
    title: "Go plugin-registry dispatch (RegisterModule -> global map -> Context.LoadModule) is not a static call edge — forward slice from main() misses all HTTP handlers"  # 572c
    status: todo_hard  # 572c
    priority: 3  # 572c
    parent:  # 572c
    tags:  # 572c
    - dogfood  # 572c
    - wave5  # 572c
    isbefore: []  # 572c
    duplicate_of: []  # 572c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 572c
    pr_ref:  # 572c
    description: "Found in DEEP bakeoff deep-20260623-134237 cohort-001 iter-004 (caddy, Go). Caddy's module architecture dispatches via a global registry: 'RegisterModule' populates a map, and 'Context.LoadModule' looks up + instantiates by string ID at runtime. Hypergumbo emits no static edge across this indirection, so the forward slice from 'main()' reaches only 13 nodes and never touches an HTTP handler / module Provision/ServeHTTP method. This is the dominant reason caddy's forward-slice usefulness is limited despite an otherwise strong Go call graph (9441 resolved cross-file calls). A registry-linker (recognize RegisterModule(id, ctor) + LoadModule(id) pairs, emit dispatches_to) would recover the plugin dispatch. Evidence: reflect/cohort-001/iter-004/caddy.assessment.yaml; slice.0.json (13 nodes from main)."  # 572c
    fields: {}  # 572c
- op: discuss  # 17de
  at: '2026-07-16T11:37:44Z'  # 17de
  by: agent  # 17de
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 17de
  clock: 2  # 17de
  nonce: 17de  # 17de
  message: "Scoping note (2026-07-16, per-language cohort wrap-up). Assessed during the 'crush the cohort in a couple mega-PRs' pass. This is NOT a bounded analyzer tweak like its cohort siblings (WI-kodap/WI-fagit/WI-kudir, all shipped in PR #689/#691) — it needs a NEW framework-dispatch LINKER, a sibling of packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/{kafka_streams_dispatch,airflow_framework_dispatch,message_dispatch}.py. There is no existing RegisterModule/LoadModule handling anywhere in the tree (grepped). The linker must: (1) detect module registration (caddy.RegisterModule(SomeModule{}) — the factory), (2) detect the dispatch read (ctx.LoadModule / registry lookup by name), (3) emit dispatches_to edges from the load site to the registered module's provisioning method, so the forward slice from main() reaches the HTTP handlers. Per ADR-3bbb it needs a Framework-subcategory docstring. Deliberately deferred from the cohort mega-PRs to keep them tight and because it warrants its own TDD + 100% coverage + bakeoff-validation cycle. Recommended as its own focused linker PR. Caddy is the canonical repro (in /tmp/f5_cohort_pool/caddy)."  # 17de
