- op: discuss  # 0083
  at: '2026-07-16T19:53:23Z'  # 0083
  by: agent  # 0083
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0083
  clock: 4  # 0083
  nonce: '0083'  # 0083
  message: "Fixed in PR #693 (dev 1965318df9). New Framework-subcategory linker packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/caddy_module_dispatch.py.\n\nApproach (refined from the scoping note by measure-live): the register->load coupling flows through a runtime string ID resolved from JSON, so a specific LoadModule site is NOT statically matchable to a specific module — that half is deliberately out of scope (same posture as kafka_streams/decorator dispatch linkers). The linker instead recovers the structural half: a Caddy module = a Go struct owning a CaddyModule() ModuleInfo marker method; emit dispatches_to edges from that MARKER METHOD to each framework-called handler (Provision/Validate/Cleanup/Start/Stop/ServeHTTP). Anchor is the marker method, NOT the struct: measure-live showed the struct is only reached by contains edges (which forward-slice does not traverse), while the marker is on the reachable chain init->RegisterModule->Module.CaddyModule->T.CaddyModule (last hop via the implements linker).\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-ran the filed repro on the canonical repo /tmp/f5_cohort_pool/caddy): the linker emits 131 caddy_module dispatches_to edges, reaching 131 distinct handler methods that were previously 0-incoming dead-code candidates. 120/136 CaddyModule markers have incoming calls/dispatches_to — i.e. the register->dispatch chain resolves IN-TREE for 88% of modules on real Caddy (cross-package import via go.mod resolves, unlike a bare synthetic fixture), so those handlers are genuinely reachable from the registration flow. Same-package minimal fixture confirms Gzip.Provision/ServeHTTP become reachable from main(). Linker + test at 100% coverage; full smart-test 3330 passed.\n\nRESIDUALS (honest): (1) the 16/136 (12%) markers without an in-tree incoming edge are the cross-package init->RegisterModule Go-resolution gap (external_symbol stub) — a separate Go analyzer concern, on which full main-reachability of those modules' handlers depends. (2) Module-namespace-specific handler methods beyond the universal interface hooks (encoder NewEncoder, matcher Match, etc.) are not yet in the dispatched-method set. Both documented in the linker docstring."  # 0083
